From: Fanasina <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475: Describe the CPU capacity and energy model

sm8450.dtsi gives no capacity-dmips-mhz nor dynamic-power-coefficient, so the
scheduler saw eight identical cores (cpu_capacity 1024 on all of them) and
the energy model could not be built. Add both for the three core types, with
the values of the vendor device tree: cpu0-3 Cortex-A510 (1024, 100), cpu4-6
Cortex-A710 (2253, 257), cpu7 Cortex-X2 (2386, 509).

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi | 47 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 47 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
@@ -270,3 +270,50 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * CPU capacity and energy model. sm8450.dtsi describes neither, so the
+ * scheduler saw eight identical cores (cpu_capacity 1024 everywhere) and EAS
+ * could not work. Values from the vendor device tree (capacity-dmips-mhz and
+ * dynamic-power-coefficient): cpu0-3 Cortex-A510, cpu4-6 Cortex-A710, cpu7
+ * Cortex-X2.
+ */
+&cpu0 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu1 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu2 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu3 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu4 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2253>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <257>;
+};
+
+&cpu5 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2253>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <257>;
+};
+
+&cpu6 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2253>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <257>;
+};
+
+&cpu7 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2386>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <509>;
+};
